    skos:altLabel "Baeyer strain"@en ;
    skos:definition "Strain due to a departure in bond angle from 'normal' values. The term is often used in the context of non-aromatic cyclic compounds in which the internal angles differ from the regular tetrahedral angle of \\(109^{\\,\\unicode{x26ac}}\\,28^{\\prime }\\); in this sense angle strain is also known as 'Baeyer strain'."@en ;
